# udev rules: hand the wheel's sysfs + hidraw nodes, and /dev/uhid for the
# logi-ffb virtual-device proxy, to the input group. The 72- rule is the
# G923 (c266/c267/c26e) PID-scoped rebind rule; the 73- rule switches the
# G923 Xbox edition (c26d) into PC mode (c26e) on plug-in, a no-op unless
# usb_modeswitch (Recommends below) is installed.
udev/70-logitech-trueforce.rules usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
udev/71-logi-ffb-uhid.rules usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
udev/72-logitech-g923-rebind.rules usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
udev/73-logitech-xbox-modeswitch.rules usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
# softdep ordering hint for the G923 PIDs, plus a narrow blacklist of the
# standalone new-lg4ff DKMS fork (files under /etc are auto-flagged as
# conffiles by debhelper, so no explicit conffiles list is needed).
packaging/modprobe.d/hid-logitech-dd.conf etc/modprobe.d/
